{"t": 30.775, "n": 37, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I wrote the triage note to `docs/tasks/i144.triage.md`. I read `task-notes.rule.md` and `documents.rule.md` before writing it. I ran no git commands, so the engine commits the file.\n\n- **Acceptance criteria:** I copied all four from the task.\n- **Existing documents:**\n  - `test-suite.spec.md` covers isolation only for the engine's own suite.\n  - `central-run-stats.spec.md` (CST-B8) says index entries are never removed.\n  - `workspace-and-concurrency.spec.md` (WSP-AC2) covers the real state root, not the home folder.\n- **Code:**\n  - `conftest.py` holds the isolation fixture, and it only applies inside the engine's suite.\n  - No pytest plugin entry point exists.\n  - No verb removes index entries or stats rows. `store prune` removes logs only.\n- **Gaps:** I listed four, all `Findable`.\n  - **G1:** the isolation rule for any test that imports the engine. The owning spec is `test-suite.spec.md`.\n  - **G2:** the verb that removes dead index entries and stats rows, with `--check`. The owning spec is `central-run-stats.spec.md`.\n  - **G3:** CST-B8's \"never removing\" sentence must name the verb as an exception.\n  - **G4:** the engine test that runs a fixture package's tests from its own folder.\n- **Covered:** no. No gap row says `Covered by`, because no spec states any of them completely.\n- **Owner decisions:** None.\n- **Route:** `Deliver: code`, `Route: discovery`. Gaps exist, so the quick lane does not apply.\n\nARTIFACT triage_note: docs/tasks/i144.triage.md\nARTIFACT gaps: some\nARTIFACT route: discovery\nARTIFACT covered: no", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "b6ca3964-b270-477a-bea8-75c7a91da29c"}
